    "narrative": "As we manage our daily game caps for this August 10th slate, **Corbin Carroll** stands out as our clear offensive anchor with a 72.47 efficiency score. His ability to capitalize on the scarcest category, stolen bases, combined with a favorable lineup spot in the #2 hole against Gabriel Hughes, makes him the premier play for Ghost Ride the WHIP today. **Tyler Soderstrom** is our most compelling 1B option at 70.68; he is currently maximizing a high-ceiling park factor and a solid matchup against the volatile Freddy Peralta. Meanwhile, **Mickey Moniak** (61.62) and **Isaac Paredes** (60.10) narrowly cleared the 60-point \"Strong\" threshold, with **Mickey Moniak** benefiting from a massive 14% boost due to platoon advantages and **Isaac Paredes** gaining 5% from favorable wind conditions.\n\nThe decision to slot **Brice Turang** (58.95) into the MI spot was tight, as the optimizer heavily favored his placement in the #2 order slot despite the relatively tough matchup against Casey Mize. Conversely, **Austin Riley** (48.33) is our most marginal start, and owners should monitor the 31% rain risk in his contest, which could effectively shorten his day and exacerbate the impact of his poor placement in the #8 spot. We continue to manage our bench strictly; with **Jose Caballero** and **Josh Naylor** off today, and long-term assets like **James Wood**, **Trevor Story**, **Seiya Suzuki**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Vinnie Pasquantino**, **Zach McKinstry**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Travis Bazzana**, **Edwin Arroyo**, **Cole Young**, and **Henry Bolte** either sidelined or unavailable, we are leaning heavily on the active starters to provide high-efficiency output. **Gabriel Moreno** and **Max Muncy** hover in the 56\u201357 range, serving as stable, if unspectacular, pieces to round out the lineup while we wait for more favorable conditions to emerge for our deeper bench prospects.",
